## Useful Commands (Claude Code)
- `/review-pr <PRs>` — review PRs, return a merge verdict, detect duplicate/conflicting PRs
- `/review-comment <PR>` — review a PR and post inline GitHub comments
- `/review-fix <PR>` — fix valid review comments on your own PR
- `/cr <ticket>` — generate a full Change Request + Risk Assessment in Jira
- `/appsec-disposition <ticket>` — investigate & disposition AppSec/pentest findings against current code
- `/rca <symptom or PR>` — root-cause a production incident with code evidence
- `/jira-to-windsurf <ticket>` — analyze ticket and generate a Cascade prompt

## Cost / model note
Claude Code runs on `model: opusplan` by default here (Opus plans, Sonnet executes). Individual slash commands pin their own model via frontmatter (`haiku` for mechanical, `sonnet` for execution, `opus` for reasoning-heavy). Don't force Opus for everything — it's the biggest cost lever.

